 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Their claim (91:6-14) is glossed only as Al-Muyassar's «إذ أنكروا…». 91:31-37 is not glossed: the tafsirs differ on who is addressed (As-Sa'di: knowledge from the Torah; Al-Muyassar: the Arabs through the Quran). No scroll for «قراطيس» (the blamed act); a book for the Torah and the Quran, light for «نورا وهدى» and the prayer. No motif on Musa or the Prophet ﷺ. STAGING v4: c1 (91): the deniers of revelation (As-Sa'di: Jews and polytheists; Al-Muyassar: the polytheists) as 3 men talking among themselves at the centre of a town (no empty side they face); they speak at 91:7 and leave on 91:26, where Al-Muyassar turns the address to the Jews (As-Sa'di keeps one group), so 91:26-44 plays on the empty town. A book for the Torah (ends before 91:22), light for 91:23, geometric for the answer 91:39. The sheets (the blamed act) are not drawn. Musa and the Prophet are not shown. c2 (92): believers in a prayer hall read the Quran (book, 92:2) and keep their prayer (pray, ruku on 92:21-22); Mecca is not drawn, no Kaaba."
 },
